WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:16.310
Asthma is a lung disease that inflames
and narrows your airways.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:21.620
Normally, as you inhale air moves freely through your trachea, or windpipe

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.620
then through large tubes called bronchi

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.660
smaller tubes called bronchioles

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.310
and finally into tiny sacs called alveoli.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.780
Small blood vessels, called capillaries, surround your alveoli.

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.400
Oxygen from the air you breathe passes into your capillaries

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:48.120
then carbon dioxide from your body passes out of your capillaries into your alveoli

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.520
so that your lungs can get rid of it when you exhale.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:01:01.540
Your bronchioles expand when the air is warm, moist, and free of irritants and allergy causing substances called allergens.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:08.640
When air is cold or dry, or contains irritants or allergens, your bronchioles contract.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:14.670
If you have asthma, your airways are frequently inflamed and swollen.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:20.300
Certain substances can cause you are
inflamed airways to overreact even more,

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.620
resulting in an asthma attack.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.580
Triggers of asthma attacks are slightly different for everyone,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.880
but usually include:

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.300
outdoor irritants and allergens, such as

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:32.960
pollen

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.020
smoke

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.160
pollution

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.720
and cold weather

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:41.600
indoor irritants and allergens, such as

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:42.300
mold

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.720
pet dander

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:44.940
dust mites

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.880
and cockroach droppings

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:50.960
food allergens, such as

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:51.640
fish

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:52.840
shellfish

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:53.920
eggs

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:54.860
peanuts

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:55.820
and soy

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.020
and conditions, such as

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.300
respiratory infections

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.620
stress

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.220
strong emotions

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:05.940
and exercise.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:11.210
The symptoms of an asthma attack include:

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.600
coughing, wheezing,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.260
shortness of breath, and tightness in your chest.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:24.280
During an asthma attack (also known as a bronchospasm) the muscles around your airways tighten

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.960
and the airway wall becomes more swollen.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:32.430
Your airways also produce thick mucus that narrows them even more

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.070
making it hard for you to breathe.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.700
If you have asthma, your doctor may prescribe medications to reduce:

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:49.980
inflammation in your airways, constriction of the muscles surrounding your airways, or mucous secretion in your airways.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.760
During an asthma attack

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:59.370
you may need to use a short-acting rescue medication

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.110
called a bronchodilator.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:08.360
This medication causes your airway muscles to relax quickly and provide symptom relief within minutes.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:16.480
Since there is no cure for asthma, the
goal is to prevent you from having asthma attacks

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.720
by using long-acting, anti-inflammatory control medications.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.239
If you take them every day, they will reduce the inflammation of your airways

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:30.079
making them less sensitive to triggers of asthma attacks.

